A||||4||KitKar||Shipping an Engine||||1||
Z||000000||KitKar||09-23-2000||02:14 AM||||I am sure this has been discussed before, but I may need to have an engine shipped from Ohio to me in Phoenix AZ. Has anyone done this before? I would like to know, who exactly do I call to arrange this and how much should I expect to spend? I don't know if the sender will be able to put it on a palet and everything so I would assume not.<BR>Oh yeah, it is a 350 on a cradle. The Exhaust and radiator would also need to be shipped, but maybe seperately.<BR>Thank you Very much in advance.<P>------------------<BR>Rick Lord<BR>Webmaster<BR>http://www.KitKar.com||||reg||1
Z||000001||2xsess||09-23-2000||11:04 AM||||You could try a truck shipping company like "Burlington". I know that is who the Fiero Store used to ship my decklid.<P><BR>Good Luck!<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||09-23-2000||12:20 PM||||It has to be completely drained, cleaned, and wrapped.<P>Anything that heavy will have to be palletized. If you don't either they won't take it or the truck co. will skid it up and charge you accordingly. Pallets usually aren't hard to come by.<P>you'll have to call around for prices. You also need to specify a truck with lift gate on both ends unless you have dock or forklift access. trucking companies are all in the phone book.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Spyder||09-23-2000||02:38 PM||||I personally would have it palletized. Since it is on the k frame have it strapped down on the pallet. Try to get everything on the one pallet. Try to find a carrier who can ship it direct, or with the fewest change overs you can get. It makes shipping cheaper. Also list it as USED auto parts or equivalent. If you don’t specify they will assume new. Pay the guy shipping it to build a pallet if you have to.  Some carriers have online projected cost of shipping programs, but you will have to call on the shipping code for the used engine/auto parts. I’m sure I forgot something but this should get you started.<BR>And by the way, I'm the guy that sent you the Daytona pics.||||reg||1
Z||000004||pherder||09-23-2000||04:52 PM||||Rick,<P>IF the seller can get it on a pallet and to the airport (Groveport, OH (CMH) or Vandalia, OH (DAY) or Brookpark, OH (TOL) or Maumee, OH (CLE)), have them send it by Forward Air.<P>They will then deliver it to PHX (Phoenix, AZ) in ~ 3 days where you can pick it up @ the airport.<P>I have heard of someone shipping a fully built chopper motorcycle in a crate!  I have also heard you will not find a cheaper shipper for the weight.<P> <A HREF="http://www.forwardair.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.forwardair.com/</A> <P>Paul||||reg||1
